1
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:36,020
Mokku and Grandpa's life
together was very happy.

2
00:01:37,246 --> 00:01:38,080
But...

3
00:01:38,105 --> 00:01:40,518
...because Grandpa doted
on Mokku so much...

4
00:01:40,980 --> 00:01:41,940
...Redbeard the mouse—

5
00:01:41,964 --> 00:01:44,760
...who had been living there
long before Mokku—got jealous...

6
00:01:45,487 --> 00:01:47,299
...dragged in the wicked fox Kenken...

7
00:01:47,714 --> 00:01:50,020
...and pushed Mokku
straight into the river.

8
00:01:53,945 --> 00:01:55,229
Fortunately, Mokku was saved...

9
00:01:55,729 --> 00:01:58,026
...by the Oak Tree Fairy...

10
00:01:58,237 --> 00:01:59,877
...but Redbeard didn't give up...

11
00:02:00,011 --> 00:02:03,290
...waiting for another
chance to finish Mokku off.

12
00:02:10,561 --> 00:02:11,795


13
00:02:13,068 --> 00:02:14,068


14
00:02:15,568 --> 00:02:16,654


15
00:02:22,344 --> 00:02:23,344
Mokku!

16
00:02:28,569 --> 00:02:29,569
Where am I?

17
00:02:30,220 --> 00:02:31,274
Mokku, how's your fever?

18
00:02:31,989 --> 00:02:34,940
Ah, it's gone down.
You'll be all right now.

19
00:02:35,315 --> 00:02:37,369
Grandpa cured me, didn't he?

20
00:02:37,720 --> 00:02:43,860
Grandpa prayed to God to save you,
even if it cost his own life.

21
00:02:44,310 --> 00:02:47,512
If you aren't grateful to Grandpa,
you'll be punished, Mokku.

22
00:02:49,290 --> 00:02:52,533
I'm sorry for worrying you, Grandpa.

23
00:03:19,979 --> 00:03:21,921
Really, Pico? Congratulations!

24
00:03:22,079 --> 00:03:22,726
Mokku!

25
00:03:22,820 --> 00:03:23,550
What is it?

26
00:03:23,691 --> 00:03:25,858
What are you talking to Pico about?

27
00:03:27,590 --> 00:03:29,360
Can't you hear him, Grandpa?

28
00:03:29,765 --> 00:03:33,060
Look, he's saying his babies were born!

29
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:42,552
Oho, babies?
Well, congratulations, Pico.

30
00:03:42,864 --> 00:03:45,578
Two boys and two girls, he says.

31
00:03:47,860 --> 00:03:49,780
I bet the babies are so cute.

32
00:03:59,810 --> 00:04:06,065
Well of course they're cute!
Even to me, Mokku,you're just as precious.

33
00:04:08,330 --> 00:04:10,444
Pico, hurry up and bring them here!

34
00:04:14,170 --> 00:04:17,925
He said, "Mokku is a troublemaker,
so we don't want them playing together."

35
00:04:17,949 --> 00:04:19,506
Who does he think he is?!

36
00:04:22,340 --> 00:04:24,220
See, that's what won't do.

37
00:04:24,320 --> 00:04:26,940
You mustn't do mean things
or bully your friends.

38
00:04:27,125 --> 00:04:29,140
You have to get along with them,
no matter what.

39
00:04:30,469 --> 00:04:34,140
I know. If I don't, I won't be
able to become human, right?

40
00:04:34,790 --> 00:04:36,943
Huh? Mokku, become human?

41
00:04:37,105 --> 00:04:38,527
That's right, my boy.

42
00:04:38,551 --> 00:04:42,218
You must be a good boy, or you'll
never become a real human. Now then...

43
00:04:42,470 --> 00:04:46,147
I'll become kindhearted and
turn into a human soon.

44
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:47,500
Look.

45
00:04:48,725 --> 00:04:50,900
I can even fold my nightclothes neatly.

46
00:04:57,250 --> 00:04:59,940
A wooden puppet made of
dead wood becoming human?

47
00:05:00,701 --> 00:05:03,522
As if such a ridiculous thing could happen.

48
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:07,700
Even with all my skill,
that would be a bit impossible.

49
00:05:10,902 --> 00:05:11,952


50
00:05:12,750 --> 00:05:13,769
That little brat!

51
00:05:13,793 --> 00:05:16,924
Just moving and talking is annoying
enough for a puppet...

52
00:05:16,949 --> 00:05:19,565
...and now he wants to
become a real human?!

53
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:21,520
You'd better quit getting
so full of yourself!

54
00:05:25,863 --> 00:05:27,863


55
00:05:35,110 --> 00:05:39,180
And what does that old man see in a
cheeky puppet bastard like him anyway?!

56
00:05:39,597 --> 00:05:43,527
Listen. Hate to brag,
but with my build, my face...

57
00:05:43,551 --> 00:05:48,847
...and this long tail,
I'm way better-looking.

58
00:05:53,840 --> 00:06:00,878
Just you wait. I'll crunch him to splinters
with these sharp fangs of mine!

59
00:06:02,820 --> 00:06:05,900
Hurry, hurry! Hurry, hurry!

60
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,660
Sorry to keep you waiting!

61
00:06:13,027 --> 00:06:14,816
Wait!

62
00:06:15,020 --> 00:06:16,500
Wait, wait, wait, wait!

63
00:06:16,520 --> 00:06:17,520
You're in for a shock!

64
00:06:17,700 --> 00:06:19,101
That was too easy...

65
00:06:19,523 --> 00:06:21,523
Get outta here!

66
00:06:31,310 --> 00:06:33,320
It's all right now, Big Brother.

67
00:06:35,145 --> 00:06:39,622
You idiot, you clumsy fool,
you blockhead, you bungler, you moron!

68
00:06:39,700 --> 00:06:42,272
Look, just because you're
educated, Big Brother...

69
00:06:42,296 --> 00:06:45,914
...did you really have to rattle off
every insult in the book?

70
00:06:46,220 --> 00:06:48,077
Hmph, so what?!

71
00:06:48,101 --> 00:06:49,858
If you hadn't sneezed back then...

72
00:06:49,882 --> 00:06:52,760
...we could've stolen the chicken
from the village head's place!

73
00:06:52,940 --> 00:06:55,327
But that was because
you let one rip, wasn't it?

74
00:06:55,351 --> 00:06:58,917
It smelled so pungent,
I couldn't help myself!

75
00:06:58,969 --> 00:07:01,452
Nature calls, so what was
I supposed to do?!

76
00:07:02,090 --> 00:07:06,732
Don't make me yell. My stomach is
sticking to my back already, damn it.

77
00:07:10,671 --> 00:07:11,765


78
00:07:11,992 --> 00:07:13,078


79
00:07:14,193 --> 00:07:20,736
♪ Atama no naka made kashi no ki darake ♪
Even the inside of my head is pure oak.

80
00:07:21,080 --> 00:07:28,086
♪ Yarukoto kodomo to kawaranai ♪
Everything I do is just like a child.

81
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:31,860
♪ Dakedo dakedo ♪
But still, but still,

82
00:07:32,335 --> 00:07:34,382
♪ sabishi toki ni...  ♪
when I'm lonely...

83
00:07:34,607 --> 00:07:38,110
Well, well, that's the smell of sandwiches!

84
00:07:38,182 --> 00:07:40,900
I smell ham, cheese, and corned beef too!

85
00:07:41,100 --> 00:07:42,525
I wonder why, lick.

86
00:07:44,070 --> 00:07:45,904
Go swipe that lunch.

87
00:07:46,005 --> 00:07:49,330
But Mokku hasn't forgotten
being thrown into the river yet.

88
00:07:49,840 --> 00:07:51,981
Just blame that on the mouse.

89
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:53,988
He's the one who pushed him in, after all.

90
00:07:54,040 --> 00:07:55,420
That's not fair...

91
00:07:55,543 --> 00:07:57,240
Boss Kenken.

92
00:07:57,380 --> 00:07:59,788
Oh, Redbeard...Look, what I mean is...

93
00:07:59,812 --> 00:08:03,987
...I'm truly planning to beat
Mokku up for your sake.

94
00:08:05,450 --> 00:08:06,840
Really?

95
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:11,032
Do my eyes look like they're lying?
Huh? Well? Take a look!

96
00:08:13,135 --> 00:08:15,380
Boss, you've got crust in your eye.

97
00:08:15,835 --> 00:08:17,235
Damn it!

98
00:08:18,353 --> 00:08:20,404
Mokku's getting away!

99
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:22,125
Leave it to me!

100
00:08:40,767 --> 00:08:44,159
Oh, Mokku... Good morning to you.

101
00:08:44,405 --> 00:08:45,920
It's Hanaguro the Weasel.

102
00:08:46,642 --> 00:08:48,778
Just wait up, Mokku!

103
00:08:48,802 --> 00:08:54,158
Hey, hey, did you know they opened
a super fun game arcade in town?

104
00:08:54,569 --> 00:08:57,325
You can't trust anything
Kenken or Hanaguro say.

105
00:08:57,349 --> 00:09:01,559
Mokku, are you talking about the
time you got pushed into the creek?

106
00:09:01,780 --> 00:09:04,312
Redbeard the mouse did that, you know.

107
00:09:04,540 --> 00:09:05,649
I wonder why?

108
00:09:06,655 --> 00:09:07,802
Red Beard did?

109
00:09:08,100 --> 00:09:11,266
It pisses him off that your
grandfather dotes on you.

110
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:12,500
I wonder why?

111
00:09:13,255 --> 00:09:15,885
I've never been mean to Redbeard.

112
00:09:15,950 --> 00:09:17,880
That's just the kind of guy he is.

113
00:09:18,040 --> 00:09:21,058
If you want to be a good boy,
you have to hang out with good friends.

114
00:09:22,820 --> 00:09:24,589
Like us...

115
00:09:24,784 --> 00:09:26,119
Wait, that doesn't sound right!

116
00:09:26,435 --> 00:09:31,613
Exactly, exactly. Why don't you hang out
with us—er, with us, Mokku? Huh?

117
00:09:31,950 --> 00:09:33,310
But I have to go to school.

118
00:09:33,771 --> 00:09:35,980
Listen, Mokku. At the arcade...

119
00:09:36,165 --> 00:09:37,534
...there's even a machine...

120
00:09:37,558 --> 00:09:40,074
...that shoots out gold and silver
coins for just one copper coin!

121
00:09:40,180 --> 00:09:41,950
What? Gold and silver coins?

122
00:09:43,239 --> 00:09:45,612
Grandfather is the poorest
guy in the village, right?

123
00:09:45,636 --> 00:09:51,084
He'd be thrilled if you brought some money
home. Hey, Mokku, why is that, anyway?

124
00:09:51,860 --> 00:09:53,144
But I don't have any money...

125
00:09:53,793 --> 00:09:56,360
Well, we could lend you some...

126
00:09:56,465 --> 00:09:57,871


127
00:10:00,569 --> 00:10:02,001
Will you really lend it to me?

128
00:10:02,025 --> 00:10:03,166
Ow, ow, ow!

129
00:10:04,482 --> 00:10:06,265
Mokku, don't give in to temptation!

130
00:10:06,560 --> 00:10:08,280
You again?!

131
00:10:08,645 --> 00:10:11,589
Go straight to school!
Don't you want to become human?!

132
00:10:11,952 --> 00:10:13,765


133
00:10:14,279 --> 00:10:18,728
Hey, Mokku. Just who do
you think you're talking to?

134
00:10:19,070 --> 00:10:20,147
The Cricket...

135
00:10:21,109 --> 00:10:22,467
Huh? A cricket?

136
00:10:22,725 --> 00:10:25,080
N-No, nobody!

137
00:10:25,793 --> 00:10:27,010
Ouch, ouch.

138
00:10:27,604 --> 00:10:31,092
What's in Kenken's bag
are beer bottle caps!

139
00:10:31,311 --> 00:10:33,101
I'm telling you, they're not copper!

140
00:10:37,184 --> 00:10:41,215


141
00:10:41,316 --> 00:10:42,839
Get to school, Mokku.

142
00:10:42,926 --> 00:10:45,488
Kenken is after your lunch box!

143
00:10:46,089 --> 00:10:49,390
Ow, ow! Stop it, stop it!

144
00:10:50,869 --> 00:10:51,869
Mine!

145
00:10:52,999 --> 00:10:55,980
- Mine too!
- Quit stealing!

146
00:10:56,482 --> 00:10:58,654
Wait! My lunch!

147
00:10:58,793 --> 00:10:59,801
Bro!

148
00:11:01,012 --> 00:11:03,012
Hey, Boss, wait up!

149
00:11:03,137 --> 00:11:04,207
Wait!

150
00:11:05,871 --> 00:11:08,113
Mokku, stop it! Get yourself to school!

151
00:11:08,272 --> 00:11:11,060
This is the lunch Grandpa
made specially for me!

152
00:11:11,405 --> 00:11:12,748
Like hell I'll let them take it!

153
00:11:16,285 --> 00:11:17,285
Mokku!

154
00:11:22,140 --> 00:11:23,140
Mokku!

155
00:11:35,867 --> 00:11:41,954
- Kochaka da hoy hoy cha cha,
kochaka da hoy hoy cha cha,
- ahoy hoy ahoy hoy hoy hoy hoy hoy hoy

156
00:11:43,200 --> 00:11:44,544
Like hell I'll let you get away.

157
00:12:37,895 --> 00:12:39,325
Relax, will ya?

158
00:12:39,474 --> 00:12:43,301
Falling from up there means that Mokku
kid is smashed to pieces by now.

159
00:12:43,325 --> 00:12:48,277
Getting pampered by Grandfather
didn't bring him any luck, did it?

160
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:50,010
I wonder why?

161
00:13:02,278 --> 00:13:03,512


162
00:13:07,829 --> 00:13:08,903
Where am I...?

163
00:13:16,179 --> 00:13:18,626
I fell from so high up...

164
00:13:18,650 --> 00:13:23,134
...but nothing's broken!
That's a puppet made by Grandpa for you.

165
00:13:26,298 --> 00:13:28,480
Grandpa must be worried...

166
00:13:29,079 --> 00:13:30,827
I have to get back soon...

167
00:13:31,920 --> 00:13:34,055
Being all alone is so lonely...

168
00:13:35,056 --> 00:13:37,224
I know! I'll sing a song as I go!

169
00:13:41,958 --> 00:13:48,384
♪ Koorogi-ko wa boku no tomodachi. ♪
The little cricket is my friend.

170
00:13:49,959 --> 00:13:56,560
♪ Tottemo suteki na nakayoshi nano sa. ♪
We're the very best of pals.

171
00:13:56,584 --> 00:13:57,938
- Hehe, terechau na.
Heh, you're making me blush.

172
00:13:57,962 --> 00:14:00,320
♪ Dakedo dakedo ♪
But... but...

173
00:14:00,478 --> 00:14:01,780
- Doushita, doushita?
What's wrong? What's wrong?

174
00:14:01,805 --> 00:14:04,420
♪ Yurei nano ni ♪
Even though he's a ghost...

175
00:14:06,199 --> 00:14:09,560
♪ Hiruma detekite boku ni sekkyo ♪
...he comes out in broad
daylight to lecture me!

176
00:14:09,734 --> 00:14:13,372
♪ Mattaku yokei na- ♪
What a total...

177
00:14:13,396 --> 00:14:14,045
♪ Dare? ♪
Who, me?

178
00:14:14,070 --> 00:14:17,395
♪ -osekkaiyaki ♪
...pain-in-the-ass busybody

179
00:14:17,420 --> 00:14:19,160
- Sorya nai ze, Mokku.
Give me a break, Mokku!

180
00:14:19,185 --> 00:14:22,688
♪ La la la, la la la la ♪

181
00:14:23,299 --> 00:14:31,657
♪ Mattaku yokei na osekkaiyaki ♪
What a total pain-in-the-ass busybody.

182
00:14:31,789 --> 00:14:33,956
What's that supposed to mean?!
Calling me a busybody!

183
00:14:34,910 --> 00:14:36,315
Hmph, suit yourself!

184
00:14:45,289 --> 00:14:46,510
I'm scared...

185
00:15:01,635 --> 00:15:06,278
Grandpa, I'm scared! I'm scared!

186
00:15:06,302 --> 00:15:11,393
Grandpa, help me! I-I'm scared!

187
00:15:17,420 --> 00:15:19,310
I'm scared!

188
00:15:26,740 --> 00:15:28,620
The brat's completely fine?

189
00:15:28,790 --> 00:15:31,460
Ah, he's surprisingly tough. Wonder why?

190
00:15:32,135 --> 00:15:35,063
This is our perfect chance
to get rid of him.

191
00:15:35,087 --> 00:15:37,433
Are we just going to wait around
for him to drop dead?

192
00:15:37,800 --> 00:15:40,880
There's a woodcutter's shack
deep in the forest. Lure him inside!

193
00:15:41,079 --> 00:15:44,958
He's frightened out of his mind.
This is our chance.

194
00:16:01,380 --> 00:16:02,532
Oh, Redbeard!

195
00:16:02,590 --> 00:16:06,774
Mokku, I looked all over
for you. Thank goodness.

196
00:16:06,820 --> 00:16:09,476
Were you worried about me, Redbeard?

197
00:16:10,750 --> 00:16:12,827
You're Grandpa's favorite, after all.

198
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:16,260
If anything happened to you,
it'd break his heart.

199
00:16:16,362 --> 00:16:17,733
Thanks, Redbeard.

200
00:16:17,890 --> 00:16:20,757
To be honest, I completely
misunderstood you before.

201
00:16:20,781 --> 00:16:24,613
I thought you were in with
Kenken and Hanaguro. I'm sorry.

202
00:16:26,059 --> 00:16:31,624
I tried to get your lunchbox back from
that Kenken, but I couldn't. I'm sorry.

203
00:16:32,234 --> 00:16:33,335
Thank you.

204
00:16:33,804 --> 00:16:36,444
You really are my friend after all.

205
00:16:39,140 --> 00:16:40,240
Mokku...

206
00:16:40,529 --> 00:16:44,700
...there's a woodcutter's shack
right over there. Let's rest a bit.

207
00:16:45,389 --> 00:16:47,679
But if I don't get home soon,
Grandpa will...

208
00:16:47,703 --> 00:16:50,077
Look, your jacket and
pants are soaking wet.

209
00:16:50,101 --> 00:16:52,680
If you don't dry them off before
going home, you'll get scolded.

210
00:17:22,394 --> 00:17:24,390
Looks like there's a bird's nest.

211
00:17:24,921 --> 00:17:26,640
Might be in the attic.

212
00:17:27,912 --> 00:17:29,076
- The attic?
- Yeah.

213
00:17:36,699 --> 00:17:38,429
Why don't you go take a look, Mokku?

214
00:17:38,453 --> 00:17:41,272
I'll gather firewood in the meantime.

215
00:17:41,296 --> 00:17:44,661
Okay, I'll go see. I bet they're adorable.

216
00:17:46,589 --> 00:17:49,388
Be careful, Mokku. Don't fall.

217
00:17:49,495 --> 00:17:50,880
Thank you!

218
00:18:06,779 --> 00:18:08,754
Ah, it's Pico... Won't you come here?

219
00:18:09,029 --> 00:18:10,360
Ah! Mokku!

220
00:18:24,499 --> 00:18:27,439
Is this your baby? How cute!

221
00:18:38,390 --> 00:18:39,679
Mokku! We've got big trouble!

222
00:18:39,703 --> 00:18:42,936
- Mokku, total disaster!
- Look at that... nice...
Just hold still and let me look.

223
00:18:42,960 --> 00:18:44,569
- Hurry, hurry!
- Mokku, hurry!

224
00:18:47,632 --> 00:18:49,632
It caught fire!

225
00:18:56,709 --> 00:18:58,100
The ladder is gone!

226
00:19:11,249 --> 00:19:15,475
Wood is helpless against fire.
This ought to turn that bastard to ash.

227
00:19:40,289 --> 00:19:44,695
Mokku! My babies! My babies!
Help them! Mokku!

228
00:19:47,029 --> 00:19:50,589
Mokku! Hurry! Hurry and help!
Please, I'm begging you!

229
00:19:52,937 --> 00:19:55,906
Mokku! Hurry! Hurry up and help!

230
00:19:55,974 --> 00:19:58,460
Hurry, we don't have much time!

231
00:20:04,242 --> 00:20:08,296


232
00:21:05,989 --> 00:21:08,048
Sigh... Look at the mess you've made.

233
00:21:08,361 --> 00:21:10,332
Grandpa is going to scold me.

234
00:21:24,629 --> 00:21:26,320
The other culprit must be Mokku.

235
00:21:26,524 --> 00:21:29,146
What would you have done
if you started a forest fire?!

236
00:21:29,559 --> 00:21:32,668
We should just smash that mischievous
little puppet to pieces!

237
00:21:32,975 --> 00:21:34,029
Yeah, that's right!

238
00:21:34,110 --> 00:21:35,218
Please, wait.

239
00:21:35,242 --> 00:21:37,210
It's my fault for not watching
him closely enough.

240
00:21:37,234 --> 00:21:39,142
I'll make sure he never does
anything like this again.

241
00:21:39,209 --> 00:21:42,460
Please, forgive him just this once
for my sake. I'm begging you.

242
00:21:43,639 --> 00:21:46,460
Please forgive Mokku!

243
00:21:50,694 --> 00:21:52,020
Just this once, old man.

244
00:21:52,649 --> 00:21:55,717
If he pulls a stunt like this again,
we're smashing him to bits!

245
00:22:09,389 --> 00:22:11,739
I'm sorry, Grandpa.

246
00:22:12,979 --> 00:22:15,561
Having me around only
makes you suffer, Grandpa.

247
00:22:16,367 --> 00:22:18,420
It's fine if I'm destroyed.

248
00:22:18,820 --> 00:22:19,828
You fool!

249
00:22:30,469 --> 00:22:34,935
Mokku, you're a kind-hearted puppet.

250
00:22:34,960 --> 00:22:37,474
You saved Piko's babies, didn't you?

251
00:22:37,719 --> 00:22:39,397
You're a good boy.

252
00:22:39,907 --> 00:22:43,047
Mokku, you are Grandpa's treasure.

253
00:22:45,658 --> 00:22:47,436
Grandpa!

254
00:22:56,659 --> 00:22:57,979
Thank you, Mokku.

255
00:22:58,003 --> 00:23:00,662
Mokku I will never forget
this for the rest of my life.

256
00:23:33,969 --> 00:23:36,323
<i>Next time, learning of Mokku's
wish to become human...</i>

257
00:23:36,347 --> 00:23:39,760
<i>...Nora the stray cat
plots something terrible.</i>

258
00:23:40,795 --> 00:23:44,240
<i>"If you gouge out a human's heart,
you can become human."</i>

259
00:23:45,075 --> 00:23:47,140
<i>That is what Nora instills in Mokku.</i>

260
00:23:48,865 --> 00:23:51,980
<i>Caught targeting a young boy's heart,</i>

261
00:23:52,344 --> 00:23:55,620
<i>Mokku is nearly destroyed in
retaliation by the boy's parents.</i>

262
00:23:57,684 --> 00:24:00,220
<i>Look forward to next week's
Kashi no Ki Mokku!</i>

